# Explicit rest marker (...) in a dict pattern is redundant but valid syntax.
# [ok: v  ...] means "match any dict that has an 'ok' key" — identical to [ok: v]
# since open matching is the default. This verifies the ... marker is parsed and
# accepted without changing the matching semantics.
[match [ok: 42  extra: "data"  more: "stuff"]
  [case [let v] [ok: v  ...] v]
  ...:          99]
=== out
Int(42)
